paragraphs.source_en:
In the roots of the grasses, the sorrels, I laid my body as low;
And the pearl-pale Niamh lay by me, her brow on the midst
of my breast;
And the horse was gone in the distance, and years after years
'gan How;
Square leaves of the ivy moved over us, binding us down to
our rest.

